About gnomes heading straight for polymorph traps:

I understand that gnomes, having lived in the Mines all their lives,
would know most of the ins and outs of the dungeon.  A polymorph trap,
however, disappears the moment it is stepped on.  How then, do Gnomes
figure out their location without setting them off?  Grampa Gnome
can't say to the little Gnomelings, "'N' that thar is the old poly
trap.  Been there ever since I was a lad," because of course no poly
trap could last that long--Gramps Gnome would have set it off the
first time he discovered it.

Am I missing something?

